  "grammarTitle": "Question Tags — checking, confirming, inviting conversation",
  "grammarNote": "Разделительные вопросы (question tags) добавляются в конец утвердительного предложения. Они используются для: ① проверки информации, которую говорящий считает верной, ② приглашения к разговору, ③ выражения удивления. Главное правило: если предложение ПОЛОЖИТЕЛЬНОЕ — тег ОТРИЦАТЕЛЬНЫЙ. Если предложение ОТРИЦАТЕЛЬНОЕ — тег ПОЛОЖИТЕЛЬНЫЙ.",
  "grammarTable": [
    {
      "subject": "Positive → negative tag",
      "verb": "are/is/have/can → aren't/isn't/haven't/can't",
      "short": "+ → −",
      "example": "\"She's a linguist, ISN'T she?\" / \"You've been there, HAVEN'T you?\""
    },
    {
      "subject": "Negative → positive tag",
      "verb": "aren't/isn't → are/is",
      "short": "− → +",
      "example": "\"He isn't late, IS he?\" / \"She hasn't left, HAS she?\""
    },
    {
      "subject": "be (am/is/are/was/were)",
      "verb": "→ be tag",
      "short": "be → be",
      "example": "\"It's cold, isn't it?\" / \"They were there, weren't they?\""
    },
    {
      "subject": "have/has/had",
      "verb": "→ have tag",
      "short": "have → have",
      "example": "\"She's already applied, hasn't she?\" / \"You've met him, haven't you?\""
    },
    {
      "subject": "modal (can/could/will)",
      "verb": "→ modal tag",
      "short": "modal → modal",
      "example": "\"You can swim, can't you?\" / \"She'll be there, won't she?\""
    },
    {
      "subject": "Present/Past Simple",
      "verb": "→ do/does/did tag",
      "short": "PS → do",
      "example": "\"He studies here, doesn't he?\" / \"You went there, didn't you?\""
    }
  ],
  "grammarExtra": [
    {
      "title": "Rule: Positive sentence → Negative tag",
      "color": "#1D9E75",
      "bg": "#D1FAE5",
      "border": "#6EE7B7",
      "rows": [
        {
          "form": "\"She is clever, ISN'T she?\"",
          "example": "Positive (is) → Negative tag (isn't)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"They are coming, AREN'T they?\"",
          "example": "Positive (are) → Negative tag (aren't)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"He has finished, HASN'T he?\"",
          "example": "Positive (has) → Negative tag (hasn't)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"You can drive, CAN'T you?\"",
          "example": "Positive (can) → Negative tag (can't)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"She went there, DIDN'T she?\"",
          "example": "Positive PS (went) → Negative tag (didn't)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"I am right, AREN'T I?\"",
          "example": "\"am\" → \"aren't I?\" (special case! NOT \"amn't I?\")"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rule: Negative sentence → Positive tag",
      "color": "#003876",
      "bg": "#EEF2F7",
      "border": "rgba(0,56,118,0.2)",
      "rows": [
        {
          "form": "\"She isn't here, IS she?\"",
          "example": "Negative (isn't) → Positive tag (is)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"He doesn't know, DOES he?\"",
          "example": "Negative (doesn't) → Positive tag (does)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"You haven't eaten, HAVE you?\"",
          "example": "Negative (haven't) → Positive tag (have)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"They won't come, WILL they?\"",
          "example": "Negative (won't) → Positive tag (will)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"She couldn't do it, COULD she?\"",
          "example": "Negative (couldn't) → Positive tag (could)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How tags change with INTONATION",
      "color": "#1B8FC4",
      "bg": "#DBEAFE",
      "border": "#93C5FD",
      "rows": [
        {
          "form": "FALLING intonation (↘) = confirming",
          "example": "\"It's a beautiful day, isn't it? ↘\" (I'm sure — just checking/agreeing)"
        },
        {
          "form": "RISING intonation (↗) = genuine question",
          "example": "\"She's coming, isn't she? ↗\" (I'm not sure — I really want to know)"
        },
        {
          "form": "Keep conversation going",
          "example": "\"You've been to Almaty, haven't you? ↘\" (Let's talk about Almaty!)"
        },
        {
          "form": "Express surprise",
          "example": "\"You've never been abroad, have you? ↗\" (I'm surprised!)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Special and tricky cases",
      "color": "#C9933B",
      "bg": "#FEF6E8",
      "border": "#FCD34D",
      "rows": [
        {
          "form": "\"I am right, AREN'T I?\"",
          "example": "\"am\" → \"aren't I?\" (NOT \"amn't I?\" — doesn't exist!)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"There is a problem, ISN'T there?\"",
          "example": "\"there is\" → \"isn't there?\" (not \"isn't it?\")"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"Let's go, SHALL we?\"",
          "example": "\"Let's\" → \"shall we?\" (special tag for suggestions)"
        },
        {
          "form": "\"Don't do that, WILL you?\"",
          "example": "Imperative → \"will you?\" or \"won't you?\" (requesting)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "grammarTip": "Разделительные вопросы — два главных правила:\n① Положительное предложение → ОТРИЦАТЕЛЬНЫЙ тег\n\"She's smart, ISN'T she?\"\n② Отрицательное предложение → ПОЛОЖИТЕЛЬНЫЙ тег\n\"He isn't coming, IS he?\"\n\n💡 Тег использует тот же вспомогательный глагол, что и предложение:\n\"She IS clever → ISN'T she?\"\n\"He HAS done it → HASN'T he?\"\n\"She CAN swim → CAN'T she?\"\n\"They WENT → DIDN'T they?\" (Past Simple → did!)\n\n⚠️ Особые случаи:\n\"I am → AREN'T I?\" (not \"amn't I!\")\n\"There IS → ISN'T there?\" (not \"isn't it\")",
